# Ingenious Leonin: "{3}{W}: Put a +1/+1 counter on another target attacking creature you control. If that creature is a Cat, it gains
# first strike until end of turn." Bot1 casts the Leonin ({4}{W}) and a Savannah Lions (a Cat, 2/1) on turn 1. On turn 3 the Plains is
# tapped in the main phase (its mana is lost), so at declare attackers only four non-white Moxen are left: {3}{W} cannot be paid (CR 107.4,
# 601.2h) and the activation is refused. On turn 5 the Lions attacks beside the Leonin and Bot2's Armored Warhorse (2/3) blocks it:
# the Leonin itself is refused (another, CR 115.1); the Lions is accepted and, as the ability resolves, is a 3/2 with first strike
# (CR 122.1a, 205.3m, 702.7b), so it kills the Warhorse before it deals damage and takes none. The Plains and three Moxen pay exactly:
# nothing is left in the pool.

